  "cues": [
   [
    0.117,
    "Without control, a cell's pathways would end in chemical chaos, with some products piling up and others running out."
   ],
   [
    7.917,
    "A cell has two ways to prevent this."
   ],
   [
    10.365,
    "It can switch on or off the genes that encode specific enzymes."
   ],
   [
    14.766,
    "Or it can regulate the activity of enzymes it already has."
   ],
   [
    18.62,
    "Today is about the second way."
   ],
   [
    20.417,
    "Allosteric regulation happens when a regulatory molecule binds to a protein at one site, and affects the protein's function at another site."
   ],
   [
    29.401,
    "It may either inhibit or stimulate the enzyme's activity."
   ]
  ]
